  "placementWhy": "Good (about 10 m): scale from the 600 ft bar (819 px, 0.2233 m/px; its metre bar agrees), north up (the N mag arrow, 2003), shifted onto the database's Cenote Vaca Ha (Google) at the entrance - the passage's south-east end, where the trail leaves for the shack and parking. Checked on the satellite: the Tulum - Coba road the map draws along the cave's south-west side lands on the real highway at both ends (within about 5-10 m), the map's road to Cenote Tortaga on the track running north-east, and its access road on the path from the highway to the entrance. The coordinates printed on the map (20 16.245 N, 87 28.892 W) are about 100 m west of this: placed there, the cave straddled the highway and the drawn road fell 90-120 m south-west of the real one.",
